# pigz-ks

A fork of [pigz 2.8](https://github.com/madler/pigz) (commit `fe4894f`) that
adds the ksflate engine as compression level 10. Levels 0–9 still use zlib
and level 11 still uses zopfli; only level 10 is new.

The engine and its public C API are vendored under `engine/`, so this fork
builds standalone with no sibling checkout. They are copies of `ksflate/src`
and `ksflate/include/ksflate.h`, compiled as C++20; the pigz driver stays C.
`make sync-engine` refreshes the copies from `../ksflate` when working inside
the ksflate development tree.

```sh
make pigz       # builds ./pigz and ./unpigz
make test       # upstream tests plus level-10 round-trips
```

## Level 10

`-10` splits the input into the usual pigz chunks and sends each chunk to
`ksflate_compress()`, the public C API implemented in
`engine/ksflate_api.cpp` (canonical copy in `../ksflate`). That wrapper runs
two strategy-0 optimization passes, emits raw deflate, and handles the chunk
framing:

* the last chunk sets `BFINAL`;
* every other chunk ends with an empty stored sync marker, so chunks can be
  concatenated on byte boundaries;
* the previous chunk's last 32 KiB is passed as history, which keeps
  cross-chunk LZ77 matches and therefore the ratio close to a single-threaded
  compressor.

`-i` / `--independent` turns the history off and adds the second empty stored
block after each chunk, matching the zlib path's nine-byte independent marker.
`-R` / `--rsyncable` is honored:
each rsync block is compressed separately, with the preceding dictionary plus
earlier bytes in the same chunk as history. `-H` / `--huffman` selects the
engine's literal-only mode. `-U` / `--rle` is rejected for level 10 because the
engine has no run-length-only mode.

The engine output is deterministic: `-p 1`, `-p 4` and `-p 12` produce
byte-identical gzip files.

## Measurements

6.2 MB mixed text/noise stream on a 12-core machine:

| level | threads | time | size |
|---|---|---|---|
| 9 | 1 | 11.74 s | 718,164 B |
| 10 | 1 | 10.05 s | 634,088 B |
| 10 | 12 | 1.24 s | 634,088 B |
| 9 | 12 | 1.15 s | 718,164 B |
| 11 (zopfli) | 12 | 44.18 s | 632,902 B |

Level 10 is about 12% smaller than level 9, scales ~8× on 12 cores, and lands
within 0.2% of zopfli at roughly 1/35th the time on this input.

## Tests

`make test` runs the upstream pigz tests plus level-10 cases for the default
chunking, `-p 1`, `-R -b 32`, `-i`, `-H`, zlib output (`-z`) and zip output
(`-K`). Every case is decompressed with pigz's own test mode. It also builds
and runs `tests/engine_wrapper.cpp`, which concatenates a non-final and a final
`ksflate_compress()` segment and inflates the result with zlib.

The engine-level history test lives in `../ksflate/tests/history.cpp` and is
run by `make test` in `../ksflate`. It is not part of this repository, which
only needs the vendored sources under `engine/`.

## License

The pigz license is unchanged; see `README` and the header of `pigz.c`.
`engine/ksflate.h`, `engine/ksflate_api.cpp` and the vendored engine sources
are new files under the same license.
